1
00:00:23,070 --> 00:00:24,531
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝

2
00:00:24,555 --> 00:00:25,668
بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

3
00:00:26,426 --> 00:00:31,477
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرا

4
00:00:34,303 --> 00:00:42,952
The delegates, a few of the Arab tribes came to Madina

5
00:00:44,479 --> 00:00:50,542
to negotiate with the Khalifah(خليفه) of the Muslims, Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

6
00:00:52,202 --> 00:00:53,899
They said: We never gave up Islam.

7
00:00:55,301 --> 00:00:58,084
we bear witness and we testify that there is no God but Allah

8
00:00:58,611 --> 00:01:00,568
and that Muhammad(محمد) is the Messenger of Allah

9
00:01:01,572 --> 00:01:06,884
and we will pray to Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ, but by no means, are we going to pay you Zaka'at(زكوة).

10
00:01:11,153 --> 00:01:17,455
And these Arab tribes sent very high level, delegates

11
00:01:18,522 --> 00:01:22,863
people with some old connections with notables of Madina.

12
00:01:25,294 --> 00:01:28,756
So the Friends of this leader in Madina would stay with him

13
00:01:28,780 --> 00:01:30,912
and the friends of this leader would stay with him.

14
00:01:32,345 --> 00:01:35,405
So they weren't only negotiating with the Khalifah(خليفه) directly

15
00:01:35,429 --> 00:01:41,244
but also they had some of the notables of the Muslims, speaking on their behalf.

16
00:01:43,379 --> 00:01:45,423
 And all of this pressure was mounting on the Khalifah(خليفه).

17
00:01:46,326 --> 00:01:52,836
Plus, from a religious standpoint, it wasn't very clear to the Sahabah(صحابه) yet.

18
00:01:54,950 --> 00:02:01,427
So even Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه was discussing this with Al-Khalifah(خليفه) - Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

19
00:02:01,836 --> 00:02:05,632
Now with Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), it's not at all because he was pressured

20
00:02:05,714 --> 00:02:09,067
by some of these tribes or because he had some relationship with them. No!

21
00:02:09,321 --> 00:02:14,096
He was arguing from his understanding of the Sharia(شريعة) evidence.

22
00:02:15,655 --> 00:02:18,375
So he went to the Khalifah(خليفه) and said, and this is in Bukhari(بخاريْ):

23
00:02:20,981 --> 00:02:22,802
كيفَ تُقَاتِلُ النَّاسَ؟

24
00:02:23,913 --> 00:02:27,000
وقدْ قالَ رَسولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللهُ عليه وسلَّمَ

25
00:02:27,587 --> 00:02:32,210
 أُمِرْتُ أنْ أُقَاتِلَ النَّاسَ حتَّى يقولوا: لا إلَهَ إلَّا اللَّهُ،

26
00:02:32,622 --> 00:02:40,372
فمَن قالَهَا فقَدْ عَصَمَ مِنِّي مَالَهُ ونَفْسَهُ إلَّا بحَقِّهِ، وحِسَابُهُ علَى اللَّهِ

27
00:02:41,524 --> 00:02:44,833
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: How can you fight them.?

28
00:02:45,412 --> 00:02:47,658
When Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

29
00:02:48,332 --> 00:02:54,762
I was commanded by Allah to fight the people, until they testify that there is no God but Allah.

30
00:02:55,173 --> 00:02:59,602
If they do, then they have protected themselves, and their wealth.

31
00:03:01,887 --> 00:03:02,843
Now this Hadith(حديث) of,

32
00:03:02,883 --> 00:03:04,621
 أُمِرْتُ أنْ أُقَاتِلَ النَّاسَ

33
00:03:05,982 --> 00:03:12,637
Came in various forums, but the Hadith(حديث) is Mutawatir(متواتر)

34
00:03:13,297 --> 00:03:15,076
the highest level of Hadith(حديث).

35
00:03:16,196 --> 00:03:22,746
Hadith(حديث) that is Mutawatir(متواتر) is a Hadith(حديث) that is narrated, through so many chains of narration,

36
00:03:23,104 --> 00:03:25,253
it becomes impossible to refute

37
00:03:27,171 --> 00:03:29,672
it is the highest level of authenticity.

38
00:03:30,684 --> 00:03:34,317
This Hadith(حديث) was mentioned by so many Sahabah(صحابه), just to name some:

39
00:03:34,857 --> 00:03:37,878
Abu Hurairah رضي الله عنه, Anas Ibn Malik(أنس إبن مالك), Ibn Abbas(إبن عباس),

40
00:03:38,393 --> 00:03:43,119
An-Nauman Bin Masheer(ألنعمان بن مشير), many, I think more than 20 Sahabah(صحابه) narrated it.

41
00:03:44,206 --> 00:03:49,509
And it's in, Bukhari(بخاريْ), Muslim(مسلم), Abu Daud(أبوداؤد), Tirmidhi(ترمذي), An-Nisae(ألنسائ),

42
00:03:49,726 --> 00:03:53,681
Ibn Majah(إبن ماجه), Al-Hakim(ألحاكم), Ad-Darimi(ألدارمي), At-Tabraani(أطبراني)

43
00:03:54,744 --> 00:03:55,963
Masnad Al-Imam Ahmad(مسنداِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ).

44
00:03:58,446 --> 00:04:01,816
So the Hadith(حديث) is very strong, and the Nuss(نص) of the Hadith(حديث) is

45
00:04:01,840 --> 00:04:06,193
I was instructed to fight the people, until they testify that there is no God but Allah.

46
00:04:06,457 --> 00:04:12,203
Now, when this Hadith(حديث) is mentioned, people think that it contradicts the Ayah(آية) of Qur'an

47
00:04:12,243 --> 00:04:13,092
لَآ إِكْرَاهَ فِى ٱلدِّينِ ۖ

48
00:04:13,402 --> 00:04:14,741
There is no compulsion in religion

49
00:04:15,845 --> 00:04:18,198
because the Ayah(آية) says: There is no compulsion in religion.

50
00:04:18,438 --> 00:04:19,724
While this Hadith(حديث) says;

51
00:04:19,744 --> 00:04:23,638
I was instructed to fight the people until they testify that there's no God but Allah

52
00:04:23,662 --> 00:04:26,756
and that Muhammad(محمد) is the Messenger of Allah and in another narration.

53
00:04:27,042 --> 00:04:28,734
ويقيموا الصلواة ويؤتوا الزكوة

54
00:04:28,758 --> 00:04:31,130
And they pray and they pay Zaka'at(زكوة).

55
00:04:32,220 --> 00:04:37,344
So, how do we combine between these two Nuss(نص) - text.

56
00:04:38,364 --> 00:04:43,991
Well, there were quite a few different interpretations, given by scholars,

57
00:04:44,597 --> 00:04:48,834
referring to this Hadith(حديث), one of them is that;

58
00:04:49,962 --> 00:04:53,410
Rasool Allah ﷺ was instructed to fight the people

59
00:04:54,061 --> 00:04:58,373
until they accept either Islam or Jizya(جزية).

60
00:05:00,541 --> 00:05:03,699
So by accepting Jizya(جزية) even though they didn't become Muslim

61
00:05:03,723 --> 00:05:05,328
they have accepted the rule of Islam

62
00:05:06,551 --> 00:05:08,033
they accepted the Hukum(حكم) of Allah.

63
00:05:10,287 --> 00:05:14,993
And that the whole earth needs to be ruled by the law of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

64
00:05:15,017 --> 00:05:18,963
But then as individuals, Islam cannot be forced on them.

65
00:05:20,412 --> 00:05:23,784
So you cannot force a religion on a person

66
00:05:24,171 --> 00:05:28,416
because it's an issue that goes back to the conviction

67
00:05:28,864 --> 00:05:31,616
its - من أعمال القلب - it's something that is in the heart of a person.

68
00:05:31,948 --> 00:05:34,713
You cannot force a person to be convinced in something.

69
00:05:35,630 --> 00:05:39,388
Therefore there is no - إِكْرَاهَ فِى ٱلدِّينِ ۖ - but in terms of the law of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ,

70
00:05:39,673 --> 00:05:42,875
people need to be fought until the law of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ is established.

71
00:05:44,200 --> 00:05:47,864
Anyway, so Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) goes to the Khalifah(خليفه) and says;

72
00:05:47,888 --> 00:05:49,487
How can you fight them, they are saying;

73
00:05:49,525 --> 00:05:52,338
أشهدو ان لا إله إلا الله، واشهدو ان محمدًا رسول الله

74
00:05:52,362 --> 00:05:54,546
And they're praying, how can you fight them?

75
00:05:57,269 --> 00:06:01,173
Now, neither did Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) nor did Umar(عُمَر)

76
00:06:01,311 --> 00:06:03,956
hear about the different narration of the Hadith(حديث)

77
00:06:03,980 --> 00:06:06,333
that says and they pray and they pay Zaka'at(زكوة),

78
00:06:06,642 --> 00:06:08,629
because if they did, then there wouldn't be any argument.

79
00:06:09,960 --> 00:06:12,212
What was the responsible of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه?

80
00:06:12,311 --> 00:06:12,969
He said;

81
00:06:14,492 --> 00:06:19,646
واللهِ لَأُقاتِلَنَّ مَن فرَّق بيْنَ الصَّلاةِ والزَّكاةِ؛

82
00:06:19,892 --> 00:06:29,640
فإنَّ الزكاةَ حَقُّ المالِ ، واللهِ لو مَنَعُونِي عَنَاقًا كانوا يُؤَدُّونها إلى رسولِ الله صلَّى اللهُ عليه وسلَّمَ لَقاتَلْتُهم على مَنْعِها

83
00:06:30,480 --> 00:06:36,307
He said: In the name of Allah, I will fight whoever differentiates between Salah(صلاة) and Zaka'at(زكوة).

84
00:06:37,140 --> 00:06:39,966
 And if they prevent me one camel

85
00:06:40,005 --> 00:06:45,347
and in another narration, a rope that you tie the neck of a camel with if they prevent me that

86
00:06:45,384 --> 00:06:48,325
and they used to pay it Rasool Allah ﷺ, I'm gonna fight them over it.

87
00:06:49,297 --> 00:06:50,325
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said;

88
00:06:50,743 --> 00:06:53,215
When I saw the conviction of Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق)

89
00:06:54,758 --> 00:06:56,349
I realized that this is the truth.

90
00:06:57,314 --> 00:07:02,545
So again Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) here is setting the rules for the Khulafa(خلفاء) after him.

91
00:07:03,460 --> 00:07:10,976
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) here is wondering whether a person after the Prophet Muhammadﷺ has a right

92
00:07:11,530 --> 00:07:14,641
 to fight against people who are claiming to be Muslim,

93
00:07:14,680 --> 00:07:18,489
but they're not fulfilling all of the Ahkaam(أحكام) of Islam, Al-Faraidh(ألفرائض).

94
00:07:19,037 --> 00:07:20,474
But Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) is saying that

95
00:07:20,498 --> 00:07:23,285
that is part of the authority of the Khalifah(خليفه).

96
00:07:23,956 --> 00:07:28,663
That is part of the authority of the person, who is taking the position of Rasool Allah ﷺ after he passes away.

97
00:07:30,050 --> 00:07:35,923
And he is telling the Khulafah(خلفاء) after him, that it is your responsibility to enforce the law of Islam,

98
00:07:36,463 --> 00:07:38,965
 even if the people who break it claim to be Muslim.

99
00:07:40,047 --> 00:07:45,777
So this is another case an example where the Fiqh(فقه) of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه prevails

100
00:07:46,396 --> 00:07:48,093
 and it is established as Al-Haqq(ألحق)

101
00:07:48,621 --> 00:07:50,882
even by the people who are against him like Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب).

102
00:07:50,906 --> 00:07:54,943
Umar(عُمَر) said, that I came to realize that his opinion was right opinion.

103
00:07:55,665 --> 00:08:00,949
So all of these again are issues relating to the Islamic politics

104
00:08:00,973 --> 00:08:01,603
if you could call it

105
00:08:01,643 --> 00:08:05,587
or the authority that is given to the Muslim leader.

106
00:08:07,535 --> 00:08:09,510
So Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is establishing a Sunnah(سنة)

107
00:08:11,827 --> 00:08:17,620
he made this clear to all of the delegates and they left without any agreement.

108
00:08:19,124 --> 00:08:24,066
Now Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), he went to Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه and he said;

109
00:08:25,016 --> 00:08:29,627
يا خليفة رسول الله تعلف الناس ورفق بهم

110
00:08:31,108 --> 00:08:33,819
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: O, Khalifah(خليفه) of Rasool Ullah

111
00:08:34,182 --> 00:08:35,022
تعلف الناس

112
00:08:35,094 --> 00:08:36,182
bring them close,

113
00:08:36,356 --> 00:08:37,221
ورفق بهم

114
00:08:37,261 --> 00:08:38,359
be lenient with them.

115
00:08:39,704 --> 00:08:42,415
You know, because of the condition that we are in,

116
00:08:42,606 --> 00:08:45,331
you need to be lenient, you need to give and take with the people,

117
00:08:45,923 --> 00:08:47,654
you need to show them a soft side.

118
00:08:49,955 --> 00:08:57,833
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه obviously you would find this statement strange to come from Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب)

119
00:08:57,933 --> 00:08:59,356
thats not the Umar(عمر) that we know.

120
00:08:59,844 --> 00:09:04,791
But Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was keeping in mind the circumstances of the situation,

121
00:09:04,831 --> 00:09:07,700
I mean, Madina is in danger

122
00:09:07,724 --> 00:09:09,202
the entire religion is in danger,

123
00:09:09,242 --> 00:09:10,853
the Muslim community is in danger

124
00:09:11,845 --> 00:09:14,989
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) is not saying to negotiate on issues of religion

125
00:09:15,328 --> 00:09:19,465
but he's just saying that, be a bit more lenient with these tribes

126
00:09:20,032 --> 00:09:22,515
they are claiming to be Muslim.

127
00:09:22,969 --> 00:09:26,627
So, give and take with them and try to reach a deal.

128
00:09:27,874 --> 00:09:29,256
What was the response of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر)?

129
00:09:29,532 --> 00:09:33,260
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) grabbed the beard of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) and he said;

130
00:09:33,285 --> 00:09:37,883
يا أبن الخطاب : ألجبارٌ في الجاهلية خوارٌ في الإسلام

131
00:09:38,520 --> 00:09:43,137
He said: O, Son of Khattab(خطاب), you were a tyrant, before you became Muslim.

132
00:09:43,610 --> 00:09:48,597
And now when you became Muslim, you want to become lame, feeble and weak.

133
00:09:50,031 --> 00:09:50,909
And then he said;

134
00:09:51,772 --> 00:09:55,081
إنه قد انقطع الوحي وتم الدين أينقص وأنا حي ؟

135
00:09:55,781 --> 00:09:59,969
He said, the religion has been left by Muhammadﷺ complete.

136
00:10:00,294 --> 00:10:03,588
Do you think that I will allow it to decrease, while I'm still alive.

137
00:10:04,795 --> 00:10:08,063
I'm not gonna allow the religion of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ to diminish.

138
00:10:08,419 --> 00:10:11,329
I'm not gonna allow it to go down while I'm still alive.

139
00:10:12,255 --> 00:10:14,966
As long as I'm alive, I'm going to fight for this religion.

140
00:10:15,595 --> 00:10:20,154
So, Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه whom the other tribes were calling him

141
00:10:20,403 --> 00:10:25,646
the father of the Young Camel was proving to be a different person than who they thought.

142
00:10:29,251 --> 00:10:32,414
 Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق), then went out to the Sahabah(صحابه) after the delegates left

143
00:10:32,454 --> 00:10:32,924
and he told them:

144
00:10:33,880 --> 00:10:38,399
إن الارض كافرة، وقد رأى وفدهم منكم قلة،

145
00:10:39,336 --> 00:10:42,622
وإنكم لا تدرون ليلا يأتون أم نهارا

146
00:10:43,486 --> 00:10:49,810
وأدناهم منكم على بريد، وقد كان القوم يؤملون أن نقبل منهم ونوادعهم

147
00:10:50,082 --> 00:10:54,907
 وقد أبينا عليهم، فاستعدوا وأعدوا

148
00:10:56,664 --> 00:10:59,099
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) after he gathered the Muslims. He said;

149
00:10:59,318 --> 00:11:05,483
The land has sunk into disbelief and their delegation has seen that you are few

150
00:11:06,047 --> 00:11:10,682
so that you would be unaware whether you were approached by day or by night.

151
00:11:11,335 --> 00:11:14,232
The nearest of them is only a stage from you,

152
00:11:14,595 --> 00:11:19,072
the people who are hoping that we would accept them and be reconciled with them

153
00:11:19,316 --> 00:11:23,250
but we refuse them and dissolve their treaty, so get ready.

154
00:11:24,179 --> 00:11:27,823
He said: They wanted to make a treaty with us, we refused

155
00:11:28,162 --> 00:11:31,584
and they've came to Madina and they have seen how few we are.

156
00:11:31,608 --> 00:11:34,853
Because when they saw the army of Usama(أسامه) they thought that

157
00:11:35,802 --> 00:11:37,711
there might be this huge army in Madina

158
00:11:37,735 --> 00:11:39,757
but now when they came to Madina, they saw the reality.

159
00:11:40,330 --> 00:11:41,730
There weren't many people there.

160
00:11:42,039 --> 00:11:46,874
So, the weakness of the Muslims was exposed in terms of their lack of numbers.

161
00:11:47,745 --> 00:11:50,970
And he said: Be ready, because they could attack us at any moment.

162
00:11:51,521 --> 00:11:54,226
What was the plan of As-Siddique رضي الله عنه to defend Islam.?

163
00:11:55,777 --> 00:11:59,189
Number one, he had the soldiers sleep in the Masjid(مسجد) camp in the Masjid(مسجد),

164
00:11:59,229 --> 00:12:02,718
 so that they could be ready at any moment to immediately protect Al-Madina.

165
00:12:02,937 --> 00:12:05,985
He doesn't want everybody to be in their house.

166
00:12:07,244 --> 00:12:12,756
He had the force ready, and they established their base in Al-Masjid Al-Nabwi(ألمسجد النبوي)

167
00:12:13,315 --> 00:12:13,838
that's number one.

168
00:12:13,869 --> 00:12:14,652
Number two,

169
00:12:15,191 --> 00:12:20,874
he had guards on all of the mountain passes on all of the routes leading into Madina,

170
00:12:21,136 --> 00:12:26,558
so that they would give an advanced warning to the Muslims in Madina, in case there's any attack.

171
00:12:27,469 --> 00:12:32,104
And he appointed the Umara'a(أمراء) over these guards Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب)

172
00:12:32,136 --> 00:12:34,307
and Az-Zubair Bin Awwam(ألزبير بن عوام), Talha Bin Obaid-Ellah(طلحة بن عبيدالله)

173
00:12:34,331 --> 00:12:36,870
and Sa'ad Bin Abi Waqas(سعدإبن أبي وقاص), Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف)

174
00:12:37,166 --> 00:12:38,347
and Abdullah Bin Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود).

175
00:12:38,631 --> 00:12:44,655
These were the heads of the security guards that were surrounding Madina from every direction.

176
00:12:45,131 --> 00:12:51,782
And number three, he tried to mobilize the Arab tribes surrounding Madina, who are still Muslim

177
00:12:51,869 --> 00:12:53,847
like Ghaffar(غفار) and Juhaina(جهينه) and Aslam(أسلم).

178
00:12:55,476 --> 00:12:58,166
And these Bedouin tribes did support,

179
00:12:58,484 --> 00:13:02,182
 for example, Juhaina(جهينه) they sent many camels into Madina

180
00:13:02,222 --> 00:13:08,291
and they put them under the hand of Al-Khalifah رضي الله عنه to use however, he sees appropriate

181
00:13:08,577 --> 00:13:10,581
so they did offer some help.

182
00:13:12,224 --> 00:13:14,658
Within three days, as the Khalifah(خليفه) expected

183
00:13:15,514 --> 00:13:20,888
 the tribes who were just in Madina, did prepare an army to attack.

184
00:13:21,658 --> 00:13:30,005
And they made their move, so the Sahabah(صحابه) who faced them were fighting them on camels.

185
00:13:31,473 --> 00:13:37,916
 Now the enemy has found this innovative way of scaring the camels.

186
00:13:37,956 --> 00:13:42,486
They use these like balloons made out of skin, animal skin.

187
00:13:43,412 --> 00:13:48,437
Balloons that they would fill and then they would throw these balloons

188
00:13:48,621 --> 00:13:50,666
and roll them in front of the camels

189
00:13:51,757 --> 00:13:55,933
and they would kick them, so these would roll down in front of the camels

190
00:13:55,957 --> 00:13:58,359
and that would terrify the camels and the camels would runaway.

191
00:13:59,332 --> 00:14:04,945
It was so bad that the camels just turned around and went back to Madina,

192
00:14:05,856 --> 00:14:07,313
along with all of the Sahabah(صحابه).

193
00:14:08,442 --> 00:14:12,872
So the camels got out of control and the Sahabah(صحابه) weren't able to bring them back.

194
00:14:15,197 --> 00:14:19,890
This made the enemy, think that the Muslims are weak and that they ran away.

195
00:14:20,449 --> 00:14:25,341
So, it was the Qadar(قَدَر) of Allah that, they be dragged to Madina, that way.

196
00:14:27,547 --> 00:14:31,653
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه in the meanwhile, was preparing a huge army

197
00:14:31,774 --> 00:14:38,410
and he led it by himself, and they went out under the cover of night to ambush the enemy

198
00:14:39,283 --> 00:14:42,909
 and the enemy did not know that the Muslims were coming,

199
00:14:42,949 --> 00:14:45,275
 they didn't expect that the Muslims will come out to meet them.

200
00:14:46,170 --> 00:14:49,820
And suddenly out of nowhere, the Muslims attack them from every direction

201
00:14:50,144 --> 00:14:52,445
right before Fajr(فجر), when it was still dark

202
00:14:53,356 --> 00:14:59,400
so by the time the sun was rising, the enemy was already turning their backs and running away.

203
00:14:59,995 --> 00:15:02,701
 And that was the first victory that occurred,

204
00:15:02,844 --> 00:15:05,288
and that was, what they have called Bidaya-Tul-Fath(بدائية الفتح)

205
00:15:05,328 --> 00:15:07,272
that was the beginning of the opening.

206
00:15:07,659 --> 00:15:15,738
The news spread, so in that same night the Sahabah(صحابه) in Madina would see some people coming to Madina

207
00:15:16,334 --> 00:15:20,047
and they would always assume that it is an enemy attacking

208
00:15:20,738 --> 00:15:24,265
and Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه tell them: No! This is good news.

209
00:15:25,277 --> 00:15:28,026
And they would find out that it is people bringing their Zaka'at(زكوة)

210
00:15:28,983 --> 00:15:32,015
some of these tribes coming to pay their Zaka'at(زكوة).

211
00:15:32,510 --> 00:15:35,455
One tribe came and delivered their Zaka'at(زكوة) in the beginning of the night

212
00:15:36,162 --> 00:15:41,171
a second tribe middle of the night, and third tribe, towards the last hours of the night.

213
00:15:41,675 --> 00:15:45,349
So immediately within one day, things were changing, and turning around.

214
00:15:46,064 --> 00:15:48,645
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه went to fight again.

215
00:15:49,118 --> 00:15:52,282
Ali Ibn Abi Talib رضي الله عنه and the Sahabah(صحابه), they went to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and said;

216
00:15:52,661 --> 00:15:56,952
You should not go out and fight yourself, appoint somebody to lead the armies

217
00:15:57,309 --> 00:16:00,779
because if you are killed, that will be very difficult for the Muslims

218
00:16:01,103 --> 00:16:03,641
and that will be a great victory for the enemies of Allah.

219
00:16:04,779 --> 00:16:09,867
Have somebody else, go out and lead the battles - the armies.

220
00:16:10,214 --> 00:16:13,589
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said: No! I'm not gonna stand behind

221
00:16:13,859 --> 00:16:16,786
and I'm gonna give you an example, through my own self.

222
00:16:18,330 --> 00:16:23,088
So the old man, who has already passed the age of 60

223
00:16:23,670 --> 00:16:26,032
is leading the war by himself and fighting

224
00:16:26,482 --> 00:16:30,053
and he did that in three consecutive campaigns رضي الله عنه.

225
00:16:32,643 --> 00:16:33,737
Zarrar Ibn Azwar(ضراربن الأزور)

226
00:16:34,772 --> 00:16:37,906
to show you how Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was handling the situation.

227
00:16:37,930 --> 00:16:40,516
I mean, these are events that are happening so fast.

228
00:16:41,182 --> 00:16:44,148
The death of Rasool Allah ﷺ, the appointment of the Khalifah(خليفه), the Riddah(ردَّة)

229
00:16:44,521 --> 00:16:45,858
the war against the Murtaddeen(مرتدين).

230
00:16:45,898 --> 00:16:54,964
The news coming from every corner of Arabia about armies amassing and getting prepared to attack the Muslims

231
00:16:55,191 --> 00:16:59,610
and how would Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) deal with all of this disastrous news

232
00:17:00,138 --> 00:17:01,822
that was coming from every direction.

233
00:17:02,127 --> 00:17:09,118
Zarrar Ibn Azwar(ضراربن الأزور), who was the one leading the campaign towards the north east against Tulaiha Al-Asdi(طليحه ألأسدي),

234
00:17:09,158 --> 00:17:13,764
 Tulaiha Al-Asdi(طليحه ألأسدي) is one of three who claimed to be Prophets during the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ

235
00:17:14,291 --> 00:17:17,387
and the situation only got worse, when Rasool Allah ﷺ passed away.

236
00:17:18,015 --> 00:17:21,021
The Da'wah(دعوة) of Tulaiha(طليحه) was spreading like wildfire.

237
00:17:21,554 --> 00:17:29,245
So his army was increasing every day, he was getting more and more soldiers.

238
00:17:29,687 --> 00:17:34,889
So Zarrar Ibn Azwar(ضراربن الأزور), a Sahabi(صحابي), who was appointed to lead an army to fight Tulaiha(طليحه).

239
00:17:35,137 --> 00:17:39,456
He would come back to Al-Madina and deliver news to Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

240
00:17:39,773 --> 00:17:40,576
And he would say;

241
00:17:41,307 --> 00:17:46,597
فما رأيت أحدا  ليس رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم  أملا بحرب شعواء من أبى بكر

242
00:17:46,788 --> 00:17:50,732
فجعلنا نخبره ولك أنَّما نخبره بما له لا ما عليه

243
00:17:51,556 --> 00:17:55,356
He said: I've never seen anybody, after Rasool Allah ﷺ

244
00:17:55,775 --> 00:18:01,374
who was so calm in the face of disaster like Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

245
00:18:01,683 --> 00:18:04,139
I would deliver to him the news Tulaiha Al-Asdi(طليحه ألأزدي)

246
00:18:04,667 --> 00:18:08,753
and it would appear as if I'm giving him glad tidings and not giving him bad news.

247
00:18:10,780 --> 00:18:14,047
So they would ask Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, they would later tell him,

248
00:18:14,887 --> 00:18:22,873
لقد نزل بك مالو نزل بالجبال لهاضها وبالبحار لغاظها ومانراك ضعفت

249
00:18:23,588 --> 00:18:28,365
They told him: You are carrying a load on your shoulder that was so heavy

250
00:18:28,823 --> 00:18:32,670
if it was placed on top of a mountain it would break it

251
00:18:33,205 --> 00:18:37,814
and if it was placed on the oceans, it would empty them of their water.

252
00:18:38,209 --> 00:18:40,050
and we never saw that you became weak.

253
00:18:40,617 --> 00:18:42,606
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said;

254
00:18:42,828 --> 00:18:47,217
I never felt fear in my heart after that day in the cave with Rasool Allah ﷺ.

255
00:18:48,643 --> 00:18:52,648
That day I was afraid, I told Rasool Allah ﷺ:

256
00:18:53,746 --> 00:18:57,928
If one of them would just look beneath their feet, they would see us

257
00:18:58,534 --> 00:19:03,903
 Rasool Allah ﷺ told me what do you think about two and Allah is their third

258
00:19:04,290 --> 00:19:05,773
and Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says;

259
00:19:06,278 --> 00:19:08,545
فأنزل سكينته عليه

260
00:19:09,096 --> 00:19:11,601
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has brought down His tranquility,

261
00:19:11,858 --> 00:19:16,349
so the tranquility came on both Rasool Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

262
00:19:16,511 --> 00:19:19,042
So how can Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) feel any fear

263
00:19:19,257 --> 00:19:23,026
after Allah سبحانه وتعالى has brought his tranquility on both of them in the cave.

264
00:19:23,791 --> 00:19:31,848
He said: I never felt fear after that and that's how calm and steadfast he was, in the face of all of these storms.

265
00:19:33,818 --> 00:19:39,943
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه adopted many methods in fighting Al-Murtaddeen(ألمرتدين).

266
00:19:40,822 --> 00:19:44,678
He sent 11 armies to fight in different corners.

267
00:19:45,503 --> 00:19:54,007
He also employed the method of strengthening the Muslims within the apostate tribes

268
00:19:54,481 --> 00:19:59,979
because apostasy wasn't like a movement where everybody just gave up Islam.

269
00:20:01,296 --> 00:20:04,532
In some cases, an entire tribe would give up Islam.

270
00:20:05,232 --> 00:20:09,117
In some cases, the majority of the tribe.

271
00:20:09,824 --> 00:20:11,774
In some cases the minority of the tribe.

272
00:20:12,340 --> 00:20:15,350
In some cases, tribes were firm and steadfast on Islam.

273
00:20:16,160 --> 00:20:21,039
So whenever Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه would hear about a tribe that became apostate

274
00:20:21,410 --> 00:20:24,460
he would try to establish links with the Muslims within

275
00:20:25,277 --> 00:20:31,261
and delegate to them the responsibility of bringing the tribe back to Islam and fighting them

276
00:20:31,914 --> 00:20:35,599
because he wants to reduce the load on Al-Ansaar(أنْصَار) and Muhajireen(مهاجرين).

277
00:20:35,728 --> 00:20:41,569
The Muhajireen(مهاجرين) and Al-Ansaar(أنْصَار) cannot fight in the same time, each and every tribe

278
00:20:42,112 --> 00:20:45,976
so he tried to delegate it, for example, with Yemen.

279
00:20:46,456 --> 00:20:50,360
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه did not sent any army to deal with Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي)

280
00:20:50,677 --> 00:20:55,412
rather he tried to establish links with the Mo'mineen(مؤمنين), who were within.

281
00:20:57,263 --> 00:21:03,159
Because he wanted to devote the strongest forces to fight the most dangerous Riddah(ردَّة)

282
00:21:03,183 --> 00:21:05,079
which was the Riddah(ردَّة) of Musailimah Al-Kazzab(مسيلمه لألكذاب)

283
00:21:05,579 --> 00:21:06,942
and Tulaiha Al-Asdi(طليحه ألأزدي) at the time.

284
00:21:08,595 --> 00:21:11,902
Because you have Musaylimah(مسيلمه), you have Tulaiha Al-Asdi(طليحه ألأزدي)

285
00:21:12,294 --> 00:21:15,809
and you had Sajjah(سجاح) in the north and then you had Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي) in Yemen.

286
00:21:17,251 --> 00:21:23,711
He also used the method of letters, he would send out letters, giving Da'wah(دعوة) to the Murtaddeen(مرتدين)

287
00:21:24,188 --> 00:21:29,552
 and making it clear to them that I can expect nothing from you, less than Islam.

288
00:21:30,892 --> 00:21:35,888
And if you don't come back to the folds of the religion, then you're going to face the sword.

289
00:21:36,486 --> 00:21:38,412
He was making those terms very clear to them.

290
00:21:40,432 --> 00:21:41,975
Let's start with Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي),

291
00:21:43,339 --> 00:21:47,272
Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي) was from Al-Ans(ألعنس) close to San'a(صنعاء) in Yemen.

292
00:21:48,690 --> 00:21:53,344
He claimed Prophethood during the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ in the 10th year of Hijrah(هجرة).

293
00:21:54,536 --> 00:21:59,049
And he used to receive Wahii(وحي) from Shiyateen(شياطين)

294
00:21:59,467 --> 00:22:03,886
 the man was connected to Devil's, he was possessed by demons.

295
00:22:05,375 --> 00:22:11,859
He started out his mission in the beginning, secretly, and then he announced it

296
00:22:13,550 --> 00:22:18,890
and suddenly, his Da'wah(دعوة) was spreading very fast.

297
00:22:19,722 --> 00:22:24,960
In the beginning it engulfed all of his people of Al-Ans(ألعنس), and then it started spreading out

298
00:22:25,222 --> 00:22:27,626
and he advanced towards San'a(صنعاء).

299
00:22:28,384 --> 00:22:31,199
And he fought with Shahar Bin Badhan(شهر بن باذان).

300
00:22:31,628 --> 00:22:36,160
When Yemen became Muslim - San'a(صنعا) was ruled by a Persian family.

301
00:22:37,466 --> 00:22:43,750
Because Yemen was invaded for some time Abraha(أبرهة) invaded Yemen, Abraha Al-Ashram(أبرهة ألأشرم).

302
00:22:44,176 --> 00:22:47,862
So then they sought assistance from the Persian Empire to help them.

303
00:22:47,886 --> 00:22:52,966
So, the Persian sent an army to Yemen, which fought Abraha(أبرهة) and defeated him

304
00:22:53,407 --> 00:22:58,471
and then they took over, so there were remnants of Persians, in Yemen.

305
00:22:59,131 --> 00:23:03,914
When Rasool Allah ﷺ sent them letters inviting them to Islam

306
00:23:04,285 --> 00:23:05,605
these Persians became Muslim.

307
00:23:05,734 --> 00:23:09,024
Badhan(باذان), who was governing San'a(صنعاء) at that time, he became Muslim

308
00:23:10,513 --> 00:23:16,455
and Rasool Allah ﷺ approved him in his position of being the governor of San'a(صنعاء).

309
00:23:18,053 --> 00:23:21,164
And Rasool Allah ﷺ appointed him to govern all of Yemen.

310
00:23:21,254 --> 00:23:25,859
When he passed away, Rasool Allah ﷺ split up, Yemen in to different states

311
00:23:26,793 --> 00:23:30,557
and his son continued ruling over San'a(صنعاء), his son, his name is Shahar(شهر).

312
00:23:31,663 --> 00:23:34,144
Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي) was now marching towards San'a(صنعاء).

313
00:23:35,170 --> 00:23:39,648
And he met with Shahar Bin Badhan(شهر بن باذان) in Shuoob(شعوب), which is next to San'a(صنعاء).

314
00:23:40,357 --> 00:23:44,414
And he defeated him, so now Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي) is ruling over San'a(صنعاء).

315
00:23:45,028 --> 00:23:47,991
And then he was sending his army so he was able to take over Najraan(نجران)

316
00:23:48,573 --> 00:23:50,541
and he was able to reach into Lahaj(لحج).

317
00:23:50,800 --> 00:23:54,940
So, his control was getting larger and larger.

318
00:23:56,028 --> 00:24:03,396
Rasool Allah ﷺ sent a message to his Umara'a(أمراء) in Yemen

319
00:24:03,893 --> 00:24:10,441
to deal with the situation of Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي), either by deception or by brute force.

320
00:24:11,369 --> 00:24:14,649
 Meaning you either take care of him from inside

321
00:24:15,049 --> 00:24:19,511
or you meet him through outside forces and armies.

322
00:24:21,171 --> 00:24:26,179
When Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي) killed Shahar Bin Badhan(شهر بن باذان) the Persian king of Yemen.

323
00:24:27,953 --> 00:24:31,497
He married his wife, Azaad(آزاد).

324
00:24:32,193 --> 00:24:35,874
And he tried to establish close relationships with Al-Abnaa(ألأبناء)

325
00:24:35,898 --> 00:24:40,621
Alabnaa(ألأبناء) are the Persians in Yemen, among them was Firoze(فيروز) and others.

326
00:24:41,811 --> 00:24:45,601
And the head of the Army of Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي) his name is Qais(قيس).

327
00:24:47,937 --> 00:24:57,166
So now Firoze(فيروز) started a plot, thinking about the plot to get rid of Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي) from within

328
00:24:57,452 --> 00:25:00,120
rather than facing him with armies.

329
00:25:00,144 --> 00:25:04,157
Why don't we try to take care of Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي) himself by assassinating him

330
00:25:04,599 --> 00:25:09,386
because the whole problem would be solved if this one figure is eliminated.

331
00:25:10,616 --> 00:25:16,075
So Firoze(فيروز) was able to gather around him, some like minded people

332
00:25:16,099 --> 00:25:20,140
who were still Muslim firm on Islam and willing to sacrifice for Islam.

333
00:25:21,917 --> 00:25:28,684
And then they went to Qais(قيس), the head of the army of Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي)

334
00:25:29,079 --> 00:25:31,604
they heard that there's a dispute going on between the two.

335
00:25:32,562 --> 00:25:34,701
So they went to Qais(قيس) and they told him,

336
00:25:35,047 --> 00:25:39,580
We are willing to work with you to get rid of Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي) and Qais(قيس) agreed.

337
00:25:39,819 --> 00:25:44,484
Now Qais(قيس) might not have necessarily agreed because he wants to go back to Islam

338
00:25:45,066 --> 00:25:49,489
it is because he had a political dispute over power with Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي).

339
00:25:50,079 --> 00:25:52,272
And he was afraid that Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي) would get rid of him

340
00:25:53,370 --> 00:25:56,928
and then Firoze(فيروز) consulted with the wife of Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي)

341
00:25:56,952 --> 00:25:58,262
Azaad(آزاد), the Persian woman.

342
00:25:59,595 --> 00:26:01,926
He said: This is our plan, how can you help us.

343
00:26:02,548 --> 00:26:05,915
She said: Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي) is always surrounded by guards

344
00:26:06,231 --> 00:26:10,523
they never leave him alone, until he gets into this particular room.

345
00:26:11,903 --> 00:26:15,310
So there is no way for you to reach Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي)

346
00:26:15,908 --> 00:26:19,954
unless you come from this direction and she gave them a layout of the palace.

347
00:26:20,755 --> 00:26:26,588
This particular room, where Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي) sleeps with his family.

348
00:26:27,046 --> 00:26:35,572
The only place that is free from security guards, there is a way to access it, from the outside.

349
00:26:36,732 --> 00:26:43,017
And she gave them the plan and the layout and the way of how to get into this room.

350
00:26:43,279 --> 00:26:44,750
Now, since it's late at night,

351
00:26:45,009 --> 00:26:52,683
she said: I will place for you in this particular room some light a lamp and weapons.

352
00:26:53,126 --> 00:26:59,367
Now, Firoze(فيروز) was able to get in and out and meet with Azaad(آزاد) because he was her cousin.

353
00:27:00,416 --> 00:27:02,700
 So Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي) wouldn't suspect.

354
00:27:04,052 --> 00:27:06,533
So now, Azaad(آزاد) helped them out

355
00:27:06,557 --> 00:27:09,930
and they decided that we're going to meet this particular night.

356
00:27:10,379 --> 00:27:14,207
So Firoze(فيروز) along with two other men they broke into this room

357
00:27:15,000 --> 00:27:19,749
and as soon as they wanted to get the lamp and the weapons

358
00:27:20,221 --> 00:27:23,149
Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) came to Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي) when he was asleep

359
00:27:23,489 --> 00:27:28,112
and he made him sit up upright and speak to Firoze(فيروز).

360
00:27:28,671 --> 00:27:30,569
Now Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي) he himself was asleep

361
00:27:31,167 --> 00:27:33,697
but this was Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) speaking on his tongue.

362
00:27:34,263 --> 00:27:36,729
And he was saying Firoze(فيروز), I know what you want to do

363
00:27:37,905 --> 00:27:41,618
Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي) was a huge and powerful well built Man.

364
00:27:42,926 --> 00:27:46,172
Firoze(فيروز) was terrified by Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي) speaking to him

365
00:27:46,919 --> 00:27:50,585
and he thought he initially thought that it is actually Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي) speaking to him

366
00:27:50,637 --> 00:27:52,631
but it was the devil, speaking to him.

367
00:27:54,088 --> 00:28:00,095
So he said: If I retreat now then our plan is over with

368
00:28:00,451 --> 00:28:03,323
and he doesn't have time to go and grab the weapons.

369
00:28:03,514 --> 00:28:05,609
So he just jumped on Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي)

370
00:28:06,062 --> 00:28:11,680
and got on top of him and grabbed his head and broke his neck and then he walked out.

371
00:28:11,965 --> 00:28:14,982
Azaad(آزاد) thought that he's running away.

372
00:28:15,006 --> 00:28:16,173
She told him: Where are you going?

373
00:28:16,213 --> 00:28:17,511
She didn't know that he was killed.

374
00:28:18,201 --> 00:28:20,575
He said: I'm going to go and tell my two companions.

375
00:28:21,111 --> 00:28:23,840
So he went on call them from the other room and they came in

376
00:28:25,180 --> 00:28:27,227
to find that Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي) wasn't dead yet.

377
00:28:27,251 --> 00:28:30,087
He was tossing around in the room, even though his neck was broken.

378
00:28:31,083 --> 00:28:33,538
Allah Ho Alam(الله أعلم) it was the Jinn(جن) inside of him or what

379
00:28:33,823 --> 00:28:36,087
but he was tossing around in the room.

380
00:28:36,895 --> 00:28:39,292
So Firoze(فيروز) said: I tried to grab him, I couldn't.

381
00:28:39,317 --> 00:28:41,771
The man was so strong and powerful, who just jumping around

382
00:28:41,795 --> 00:28:44,030
so the other two had to come and grab him for me

383
00:28:44,512 --> 00:28:46,881
until I grabbed the knife and I beheaded him.

384
00:28:47,190 --> 00:28:50,450
So then we waited in the room until it was Fajr(فجر), we just stayed in there

385
00:28:51,235 --> 00:28:55,120
By the way, Firoze(فيروز) said: When he cut the head of Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي)

386
00:28:55,616 --> 00:28:56,941
he made the very loud roar

387
00:28:57,664 --> 00:29:00,833
so the guards came running and they said: What's happening.?

388
00:29:01,259 --> 00:29:02,630
So the wife of Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي) said:

389
00:29:02,654 --> 00:29:05,070
Don't worry, the prophet is receiving revelation.

390
00:29:05,840 --> 00:29:11,224
Anyway they waited in the room, till it was Fajr(فجر) - and they went out and made Adhaan(آذان),

391
00:29:12,447 --> 00:29:13,941
which was not heard in a long time.

392
00:29:15,004 --> 00:29:16,899
So the soldiers are all amazed

393
00:29:17,599 --> 00:29:24,705
and that was a sign for the soldiers of Firoze(فيروز) when they hear Adhaan(آذان) to come.

394
00:29:25,095 --> 00:29:27,746
 So the armies of Firoze(فيروز) attacked

395
00:29:28,383 --> 00:29:32,445
and they threw out the head of Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي) in front of his supporters

396
00:29:32,816 --> 00:29:35,061
and that was the end of Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي).

397
00:29:37,245 --> 00:29:43,295
The same night, the assassination of Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي) took place

398
00:29:44,072 --> 00:29:48,158
Jibreel عليه السّلام went to Muhammadﷺ and gave him the news.

399
00:29:49,061 --> 00:29:52,231
So Rasool Allah ﷺ the next day in the morning is telling the Sahabah(صحابه)

400
00:29:53,743 --> 00:29:55,417
Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي) has been killed

401
00:29:55,999 --> 00:29:58,937
and he was killed by a blessed man from a blessed family.

402
00:30:00,339 --> 00:30:02,064
They said: Who was it? He said: Firoze(فيروز)

403
00:30:02,326 --> 00:30:05,353
So Firoze(فيروز) was a blessed man

404
00:30:05,731 --> 00:30:10,516
and his family was blessed, because this was a plan that was mostly done by these Persian men

405
00:30:11,146 --> 00:30:13,169
plus, Azaad(آزاد) the Persian woman.

406
00:30:13,715 --> 00:30:16,489
So Rasool Allah ﷺ called it a blessed family.

407
00:30:16,821 --> 00:30:21,794
And by the way, this story of Firoze(فيروز) is one evidence that the Fuqahaa(فقهاء) use

408
00:30:22,416 --> 00:30:27,520
to support overthrowing a Murtadd(مرتد) government through means of assassination.

409
00:30:28,063 --> 00:30:30,164
Because Yemen was ruled by Islam,

410
00:30:30,226 --> 00:30:34,077
and then you have Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي) a Murtadd(مرتد) ruling over Yemen

411
00:30:34,706 --> 00:30:37,359
and Rasool Allah ﷺ sanctioned what they did.

412
00:30:39,004 --> 00:30:42,648
However, when the news of the death of Rasool Allah ﷺ came to Yemen

413
00:30:43,701 --> 00:30:48,068
the remnants of the army of Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي) started to revolt again.

414
00:30:50,133 --> 00:30:55,812
This time the Riddah(ردَّة) was worse because it was popping up in different places

415
00:30:56,361 --> 00:31:01,062
in Najraan(صنعاء), in San'a(صنعاء) in Hazara Moat(حضرالموت) in Kinda(كندة), in Mahra(مهرة)

416
00:31:01,754 --> 00:31:03,143
in Lahaj(لحج), in Aden(عدن)

417
00:31:03,819 --> 00:31:06,001
just as it was in the rest of the Arabian Peninsula.

418
00:31:06,653 --> 00:31:11,264
Wherever you had new Muslims, who were still weak in their faith you had Riddah(ردَّة)

419
00:31:12,503 --> 00:31:16,740
Qais(قيس), who was the head of the army of Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي)

420
00:31:17,262 --> 00:31:19,658
who joined in the plot to kill Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي)

421
00:31:20,232 --> 00:31:22,581
joined with the forces of Al-Murtaddeen(مرتدين). Why?

422
00:31:22,946 --> 00:31:29,128
Because Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه appointed Firoze(فيروز), to be the leader of San'a(صنعاء)

423
00:31:29,920 --> 00:31:33,354
and Qais(قيس) did not like that - so he broke ranks

424
00:31:33,378 --> 00:31:36,448
 and he joined with the forces of Al-Murtaddeen(مرتدين).

425
00:31:38,203 --> 00:31:41,507
So now, Al-Muhajir Bin Umayyah(مهاجر إبن أمية) and Muadh Ibn Jabal(معاذ إبن جبل)

426
00:31:41,531 --> 00:31:48,285
and other Sahabah(صحابه) who were in Yemen, they had to start fighting the Murtaddeen(مرتدين) in different areas.

427
00:31:48,691 --> 00:31:51,535
 And slowly, they were defeating

428
00:31:51,743 --> 00:31:57,956
all of the forces of Riddah(ردَّة), until the whole country fell under the rule of Shariah(شريعة) again.

429
00:31:59,516 --> 00:32:02,469
So that is the Riddah(ردَّة) of Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي)

430
00:32:02,493 --> 00:32:05,332
which again started during the life of Rasool Allah ﷺ

431
00:32:07,227 --> 00:32:09,666
I made it very brief, I didn't go into the details.

432
00:32:10,553 --> 00:32:14,829
First of all because there's a lot of names and places and events, it might be confusing.

433
00:32:15,411 --> 00:32:19,343
Second, our purpose is to learn lessons.

434
00:32:20,168 --> 00:32:25,506
So wherever I find that there are strong lessons I would mention to you the event or the incident

435
00:32:25,751 --> 00:32:28,759
because again we're talking about Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق)

436
00:32:28,783 --> 00:32:30,314
 and the era of Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق)

437
00:32:30,338 --> 00:32:32,860
and if we're going to talk about everything is going to take a very long time.

438
00:32:34,129 --> 00:32:37,251
A few events that happened in Yemen

439
00:32:37,276 --> 00:32:39,559
 and then we'll move on to the Riddah(ردَّة) of Tulaiha Al-Asdi(طليحة ألأزدي).

440
00:32:40,935 --> 00:32:44,809
The example of the righteous woman, and the evil woman.

441
00:32:45,565 --> 00:32:49,885
 Azaad(آزاد) was an example of a righteous woman

442
00:32:51,137 --> 00:32:52,498
 who sacrificed for her religion

443
00:32:53,190 --> 00:32:55,794
like Asiyah Bint Muzahim(آسيه بنت مزاحم), the wife of Firaun(فرعون) did.

444
00:32:56,853 --> 00:33:00,019
Asiyah Bint Muzahim(آسيه بنت مزاحم) was a wife of Firaun(فرعون)

445
00:33:00,718 --> 00:33:02,965
 the most powerful king on the face of the earth

446
00:33:03,528 --> 00:33:08,066
she had everything that a lover of Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) would want.

447
00:33:09,582 --> 00:33:14,367
She was living in the greatest palace, the palace which was mentioned in Qur'an,

448
00:33:14,899 --> 00:33:16,189
الْأَنْهَارُ تَجْرِي مِن تَحْتِي ۖ

449
00:33:16,213 --> 00:33:18,793
That rivers are flowing beneath me, under me.

450
00:33:19,750 --> 00:33:25,011
She had all of the wealth that she would want but that didn't satisfy her.

451
00:33:26,820 --> 00:33:31,258
And she was asking Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ to replace her with a Palace in Jannah(جنة)

452
00:33:31,282 --> 00:33:32,660
rather than this Palace on earth.

453
00:33:34,235 --> 00:33:37,152
Azaad(آزاد) was the wife of Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي)

454
00:33:37,336 --> 00:33:43,156
the most powerful man in Yemen during his time, but she was a Muslim,

455
00:33:43,660 --> 00:33:47,833
and she described her husband, Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي) by saying,

456
00:33:48,327 --> 00:33:55,089
Allah has not created any human being, more dislike to me than Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي).

457
00:33:55,256 --> 00:33:58,094
I never hated anybody in my life like I hated this man.

458
00:33:59,481 --> 00:34:05,718
She said: He does not do any good and all of his actions are evil.

459
00:34:07,371 --> 00:34:12,819
And she sacrificed, and what she did, she could have paid for it dearly.

460
00:34:13,924 --> 00:34:18,688
If the plot was uncovered by Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي), she would have been killed.

461
00:34:18,712 --> 00:34:22,536
And Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي) was very vicious, in his treatment of Muslims

462
00:34:23,066 --> 00:34:26,515
he would cut them into pieces, and let them die a slow death.

463
00:34:27,964 --> 00:34:32,044
 on the other hand, you have women of evil.

464
00:34:32,259 --> 00:34:35,823
Examples of both Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ gave the example of Asiyah(آسية) in Qur'an

465
00:34:35,847 --> 00:34:39,816
alongside the example of the wife of Lut(لوط) and Nooh(نوح)

466
00:34:40,523 --> 00:34:42,409
and both examples existed in Yemen.

467
00:34:43,687 --> 00:34:49,758
Whenever the rule of Islam, comes to a place there are going to be people who will not be happy with it,

468
00:34:50,631 --> 00:34:52,250
not everybody will vote for Islam.

469
00:34:54,274 --> 00:34:59,460
There are going to be people, who hate the law of Allah

470
00:35:00,761 --> 00:35:06,395
and believe that it is restricting their freedoms, and their liberty.

471
00:35:07,469 --> 00:35:11,678
And these people tend to be part of the aristocracy.

472
00:35:12,799 --> 00:35:20,234
People who don't want any limitations on their enjoyment and Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) and their pleasure, and their sensations.

473
00:35:21,844 --> 00:35:29,646
 There were people like this all over, in every state, which fell under the law of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

474
00:35:30,186 --> 00:35:35,304
In Hazar-al-Maot(حضرالموت) there was a movement called the movement of the prostitutes.

475
00:35:36,808 --> 00:35:41,821
This was a movement of more than 20 prostitutes from different villages in Hazar-al-Maot(حضرالموت)

476
00:35:42,615 --> 00:35:47,178
who, when Rasool Allah ﷺ passed away they covered their hands and Hinnah(هنا)

477
00:35:47,751 --> 00:35:51,763
and they sang songs to celebrate the death of Rasool Allah ﷺ

478
00:35:53,962 --> 00:35:59,318
because these were women of evil they felt that Islam restricted their life

479
00:35:59,815 --> 00:36:02,463
they were like flies, who can only survive on filth.

480
00:36:03,217 --> 00:36:08,581
And when Islam came and took away their filth, they felt that they were starving to death.

481
00:36:09,358 --> 00:36:11,655
They felt that they could not breath, they were suffocating.

482
00:36:12,269 --> 00:36:15,600
So when Rasool Allah ﷺ passed away, they were happy and they were celebrating.

483
00:36:16,652 --> 00:36:22,886
So one of the men of Hazar-al-Maot(حضرالموت), sent a poem to Al-Khalifah(خليفه), Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه

484
00:36:23,199 --> 00:36:25,458
describing the situation and asking for help.

485
00:36:26,392 --> 00:36:31,217
So Al-Khalifah(خليفه) sent a letter to his governor over Hazar-al-Maot(حضرالموت)

486
00:36:31,241 --> 00:36:33,928
Al-Muhajir Ibn Abi Umayyah(ألمهاجر بن أبي أمية) and told him,

487
00:36:34,870 --> 00:36:41,697
I command you to take an army, and to amputate the arms of these women

488
00:36:43,013 --> 00:36:48,297
and if anybody stands in your way, then deliver to them the message of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ

489
00:36:48,322 --> 00:36:50,873
and Da'wah(دعوة) to Islam, and if they refuse then fight them.

490
00:36:51,939 --> 00:36:57,844
Because Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه knew that these women are not speaking on their own behalf,

491
00:36:58,410 --> 00:37:00,865
 they are representing a certain segment of the society.

492
00:37:01,591 --> 00:37:04,168
And this segment of society will rush to defend them

493
00:37:05,508 --> 00:37:11,120
because evil always comes together to support itself whenever Al-Haqq(ألحق) attacks it.

494
00:37:12,312 --> 00:37:18,251
So all of these people of evil, who felt that Islam is depriving them of their way of life.

495
00:37:18,607 --> 00:37:21,444
They came together to protect these women

496
00:37:22,042 --> 00:37:24,965
and they marched forward to fight Al-Muhajir(ألمهاجر).

497
00:37:25,446 --> 00:37:29,069
So Al-Muhajir(ألمهاجر) spoke to them and gave them the Da'wah(دعوة) of Allah

498
00:37:29,093 --> 00:37:34,583
and told them the consequences of their actions, many of them agreed.

499
00:37:35,470 --> 00:37:37,172
And then, Al-Muhajir(ألمهاجر) fought the rest

500
00:37:37,630 --> 00:37:40,214
and then he went ahead and amputated the arms of these women

501
00:37:40,238 --> 00:37:44,798
and many of them died because of that and some other left Hazar-al-Maot(حضرالموت)

502
00:37:44,822 --> 00:37:46,858
and settled into Al-Kufa(ألكوفه) and other places, anyway.

503
00:37:47,534 --> 00:37:53,186
So every age and time there will be people who will decide to fight Al-Haqq(ألحق)

504
00:37:54,128 --> 00:37:55,222
 until the last moment.

505
00:37:57,383 --> 00:38:00,573
There was a Karamah(كرامة) that happened to one of the Awliyya(أولياء) of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ

506
00:38:01,921 --> 00:38:03,062
Abu Muslim Al-Khaulani(أبومسلم ألخولاني).

507
00:38:04,071 --> 00:38:08,511
Abu Muslim Al-Khaulani رضي الله عنه is one of the Taba'een(تابعين)

508
00:38:10,124 --> 00:38:13,751
Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي) captured him and told him,

509
00:38:14,903 --> 00:38:18,495
Do you testify that I am the messenger of Allah.

510
00:38:20,140 --> 00:38:21,309
He said: I can't hear you,

511
00:38:22,261 --> 00:38:25,650
He said: Do you testify that Muhammad(محمد) is the Messenger of Allah,

512
00:38:26,118 --> 00:38:27,180
He said: Yes,

513
00:38:28,359 --> 00:38:31,231
He said: Do you testify that I am the messenger of Allah!

514
00:38:31,415 --> 00:38:32,870
He said: I cannot hear you,

515
00:38:33,263 --> 00:38:36,045
 Do you testify that Muhammad(محمد) is the Messenger of Allah.

516
00:38:36,088 --> 00:38:40,389
He said: Yes! And he repeated that three times.

517
00:38:41,222 --> 00:38:45,259
So Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي) ordered that he be burned at the stake.

518
00:38:47,132 --> 00:38:49,646
So they burnt Abu Muslim Al-Khaulani(أبومسلم ألخولاني)

519
00:38:51,518 --> 00:38:56,692
And Abu Muslim Al-Khaulani(أبومسلم ألخولاني) came out walking without any harm whatsoever

520
00:38:57,141 --> 00:38:59,461
only the rope that they tied him with.

521
00:39:01,675 --> 00:39:07,798
So the followers of Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي) said: You have to force him to leave your land

522
00:39:07,823 --> 00:39:09,576
otherwise he will be Fitnah(فِتْنَه) for the people.

523
00:39:10,415 --> 00:39:14,572
This miracle might cause the people to go back to Islam

524
00:39:14,596 --> 00:39:18,426
so we want you to send him out of the land.

525
00:39:19,883 --> 00:39:24,291
So he went to Madina and he came into the Masjid(مسجد), and he was praying

526
00:39:25,005 --> 00:39:27,864
and Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: Where's this man from? They said: He's from Yemen.

527
00:39:28,368 --> 00:39:29,895
So he called him after he finished his Salah(صلاة)

528
00:39:30,618 --> 00:39:36,907
he said: I want you to tell me about the man who was burnt in the fire by Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي).

529
00:39:38,908 --> 00:39:40,426
He said: That man is Abdullah Bin Thaub(عبدالله بن ثوب)

530
00:39:40,649 --> 00:39:42,957
his name is Abdullah Bin Thaub(عبدالله بن ثوب).

531
00:39:43,961 --> 00:39:45,034
He said: Is it you?

532
00:39:45,581 --> 00:39:48,101
I ask you in the name of Allah, is it you? He said: Yes! It's me.

533
00:39:49,071 --> 00:39:53,149
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه immediately hugged him and started crying

534
00:39:54,223 --> 00:39:58,672
and said: Al-Hamdolillah(ألحمدلله), Praise be to Allah, who made me live

535
00:39:59,894 --> 00:40:07,035
until I see a man whom Allah سبحانه وتعالى saved from the fire just as He saved Ibrahim عليه السّلام.

536
00:40:08,304 --> 00:40:12,517
He said: Al-Hamdolillah(ألحمدلله), who made me live until I can see

537
00:40:12,607 --> 00:40:17,169
a member of the Ummah(امة) of Muhammadﷺ, who was saved from the fire.

538
00:40:17,657 --> 00:40:20,258
Just like Ibrahim عليه السّلام was saved from the fire.

539
00:40:21,270 --> 00:40:26,466
So this was a Karmah(كرامة) that happened to a follower of Muhammadﷺ.

540
00:40:27,025 --> 00:40:30,329
And it is similar to a miracle that occurred to a Nabi(نَبِي) of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

541
00:40:31,388 --> 00:40:37,279
Abu Muslim Al-Khaulani(أبومسلم ألخولاني) was one of the fascinating figures among the Taba'een رضي الله عنه.

542
00:40:38,409 --> 00:40:42,478
There are many stories about him but I'll just mention one about his death.

543
00:40:43,576 --> 00:40:49,772
He was fighting alongside Bishr Bin Arta(بِشربن أرطاة) against the Romans.

544
00:40:50,448 --> 00:40:52,395
So his Ameer(أمير) was Bishr Bin Arta(بِشربن أرطاة)

545
00:40:53,969 --> 00:40:56,369
and Abu Muslim Al-Khaulani(أبومسلم ألخولاني) was injured.

546
00:40:57,377 --> 00:41:02,748
So, before he died he called the Ameer(أمير) of the Army, Bishr Bin Arta(بِشربن أرطاة) and he told him:

547
00:41:03,892 --> 00:41:10,756
When I die, I want you to bury me, the furthest into the land of the enemy

548
00:41:12,049 --> 00:41:15,731
I want my grave, to be ahead of the graves of all of the other Shuhadaa(شهداء).

549
00:41:17,672 --> 00:41:22,722
And then I want you to appoint me as an Ameer(أمير) over the Shuhadaa(شهداء)

550
00:41:23,531 --> 00:41:26,875
and to give me a banner of war that you burry with me

551
00:41:27,879 --> 00:41:30,735
so that on the Day of Judgment when we are resurrected

552
00:41:31,107 --> 00:41:34,665
I can carry that banner and lead the Shuhadaa(شهداء) on the Day of Judgment.

553
00:41:36,692 --> 00:41:39,709
So he doesn't want his Jihad(جهاد) to stop and Duniyah(دُنِيَّا)

554
00:41:39,733 --> 00:41:44,037
 he wants to continue it in Aakhirah(آخرة), he wants to come on the Day of Judgment carrying the banner,

555
00:41:45,068 --> 00:41:46,983
 and leading the Shuhadaa(شهداء) behind him.

556
00:41:48,378 --> 00:41:52,008
So this is a Karamaa(كرامة) that happened with Abu Muslim Al-Khaulani رضي الله عنه.

557
00:41:55,301 --> 00:42:01,893
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) was very harsh with some of the apostates

558
00:42:02,608 --> 00:42:10,612
and he showed clemency to some others, depending on the situation there was not one standard.

559
00:42:12,380 --> 00:42:16,176
 Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه would make a judgment, according to the situation.

560
00:42:16,953 --> 00:42:24,013
Whenever he would see that there's potential for some people to serve Islam in the future

561
00:42:25,080 --> 00:42:26,058
he would allow them to go.

562
00:42:27,304 --> 00:42:31,097
So he gave clemency to Amr Bin Ma'diaqrib(عمروبن معديكرب)

563
00:42:31,945 --> 00:42:36,180
and Qais Bin Muradi(قيس بن مرادي), the one who was the head of the army of Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(ألأسود ألعنسي).

564
00:42:37,223 --> 00:42:41,689
He set him free and also Al-Ash'as Bin Qais(ألعشعث بن قيس)

565
00:42:42,014 --> 00:42:44,818
who fought against Sahabah رضي الله عنهم in Hazaral Moat(حضرالموت).

566
00:42:45,939 --> 00:42:47,772
And Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله)

567
00:42:47,812 --> 00:42:51,995
it was the vision of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه that he gives these three men clemency

568
00:42:52,050 --> 00:42:55,151
 because these three men played some very important roles

569
00:42:55,617 --> 00:42:58,339
during Jihad(جهاد) in the time of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه.

570
00:42:58,851 --> 00:43:02,277
See in the time of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) he gave his instructions

571
00:43:03,390 --> 00:43:07,528
that nobody, who apostated should be allowed to participate in the Fath(فتح).

572
00:43:08,610 --> 00:43:10,449
When the wars of apostasy were over

573
00:43:10,946 --> 00:43:14,567
and now the armies were sent to fight against the Persian and Roman Empire

574
00:43:15,095 --> 00:43:17,161
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) gave instructions

575
00:43:17,185 --> 00:43:20,659
that none of the Murtaddeen(مرتدين) should participate in these armies.

576
00:43:21,913 --> 00:43:25,514
It wasn't until the time of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه, was this overruled.

577
00:43:26,416 --> 00:43:28,005
And there were some reasons for that

578
00:43:28,029 --> 00:43:30,535
 if we have time In sha Allah(إن شاءالله), we'll talk about that, later.

579
00:43:33,469 --> 00:43:34,855
Another incidents worth mentioning

580
00:43:35,391 --> 00:43:37,955
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) has sent Ikrimah Bin Abi Jahl(عكرمة بن أبي جهل)

581
00:43:37,979 --> 00:43:40,227
the son of Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل), Ikrimah(عكرمة), who became Muslim

582
00:43:40,926 --> 00:43:47,814
he sent him to lead an army of 700, horsemen, to the land of Musailima(مسيلمة)

583
00:43:49,099 --> 00:43:53,876
Ikrimah(عكرمة) was in a hurry, so he got into a premature confrontation with Bannu Hanifa(بنوحنيفة),

584
00:43:54,225 --> 00:43:55,716
and he was defeated

585
00:43:57,079 --> 00:43:58,394
The news reached to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

586
00:43:59,031 --> 00:44:01,726
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) sent him a very urgent message telling him,

587
00:44:02,324 --> 00:44:05,435
 I don't want to see! Do not come back!

588
00:44:06,594 --> 00:44:09,602
Because that will weaken the morale of our forces

589
00:44:10,053 --> 00:44:12,544
and I want you to immediately leave and go to Yemen

590
00:44:13,110 --> 00:44:17,757
and to support the Muslims who are there, and to enter from Oman(عمان).

591
00:44:19,354 --> 00:44:20,635
What was the wisdom behind this?

592
00:44:20,660 --> 00:44:27,645
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه did not want the Muslims, who lost in the war against the forces of Musailima(مسيلمة)

593
00:44:27,962 --> 00:44:30,645
to meet with any army that's going to the same direction,

594
00:44:31,604 --> 00:44:37,256
because then they would share the news, and they would speak about the forces of the enemy

595
00:44:37,713 --> 00:44:41,475
and that would weaken the morale of the Muslims, who are going towards that direction.

596
00:44:42,011 --> 00:44:45,337
So he said immediately leave, and I don't want you to come back to Madina

597
00:44:45,513 --> 00:44:48,506
because this will weaken the morale of the people of Madina, go to Oman(عمان).

598
00:44:50,151 --> 00:44:54,346
You're going to fight a different battle, different field with different people.

599
00:44:54,592 --> 00:44:59,317
So go to Oman(عمان) and he came through Oman(عمان), Al-Mahra(ألمحرة) and then joined forces

600
00:44:59,703 --> 00:45:01,751
with the others Sahabah(صحابه) in Yemen.

601
00:45:02,647 --> 00:45:06,942
So that shows the wisdom in the leadership of Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق).

602
00:45:07,428 --> 00:45:09,761
When Muadh Bin Jabal(معاذبن جبل) came back to Madina

603
00:45:10,189 --> 00:45:14,599
because he was appointed by Rasool Allah ﷺ to go to Yemen to teach the people Islam.

604
00:45:15,299 --> 00:45:16,364
So when they came back

605
00:45:16,556 --> 00:45:21,962
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), his way was that whenever a governor would come back, he would sit down with him

606
00:45:23,036 --> 00:45:25,942
and go through all the records,

607
00:45:26,266 --> 00:45:34,603
and he would hold him accountable to everything that happened within the term of his governceship, Hissab(حساب).

608
00:45:35,389 --> 00:45:37,357
 When that happened Muadh Bin Jabal(معاذبن جبل) said;

609
00:45:38,296 --> 00:45:41,954
You want me to go through two reckonings, reckoning with Allah and a reckoning with you.

610
00:45:42,396 --> 00:45:45,056
I will never assume a position of leadership with you anymore

611
00:45:45,248 --> 00:45:47,550
and you never wanted to become Ameer(أمير) after that.

612
00:45:48,327 --> 00:45:51,240
He said: I'm already going to be held accountable by Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ

613
00:45:51,264 --> 00:45:52,711
and now you want to hold me accountable

614
00:45:53,426 --> 00:45:55,550
but that was the way of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه

615
00:45:55,574 --> 00:46:00,179
and Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) carried on, implementing the same rules.

616
00:46:01,129 --> 00:46:04,282
We're done with the Riddah(ردَّة) in Yemen.

617
00:46:04,771 --> 00:46:07,949
We move on to the Riddah(ردَّة) of Tulaiha Al-Asdi(طليحة ألأسدي).

618
00:46:08,508 --> 00:46:13,719
This was among Asd(أسد), Ghatafaan(غطفان) and Abs(عبس) and Dhabiyaan(ذبيان)

619
00:46:14,238 --> 00:46:15,605
the four Arab tribes.

620
00:46:17,476 --> 00:46:20,399
Tulaiha Al-Asdi(طليحة ألأسدي) was a Muslim.

621
00:46:21,982 --> 00:46:28,259
He and a delegation from Asd(أسد) came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and they said;

622
00:46:29,060 --> 00:46:34,463
We have came to pledge our allegiance to you, we are Muslim.

623
00:46:35,576 --> 00:46:41,653
And you didn't ask us to come, we came by ourselves.

624
00:46:42,876 --> 00:46:46,791
 And we became Muslim, and they went on and on bragging about it.

625
00:46:49,139 --> 00:46:50,917
So Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ revealed the Ayah(آية);

626
00:46:51,335 --> 00:46:59,806
يَمُنُّونَ عَلَيْكَ أَنْ أَسْلَمُوا ۖ قُل لَّا تَمُنُّوا عَلَيَّ إِسْلَامَكُم ۖ بَلِ اللَّهُ يَمُنُّ عَلَيْكُمْ أَنْ هَدَاكُمْ لِلْإِيمَانِ إِن كُنتُمْ صَادِقِينَ۝

627
00:47:00,685 --> 00:47:04,964
They consider it a favor to you, that they have accepted Islam.

628
00:47:05,789 --> 00:47:09,276
Say, do not consider your Islam a favor to Me

629
00:47:09,300 --> 00:47:14,776
rather Allah has conferred the favor upon you that He has guided you to the faith

630
00:47:15,116 --> 00:47:16,200
if you should be truthful.

631
00:47:16,470 --> 00:47:18,223
This is in Hujraat(حجرات) verse 17.

632
00:47:19,306 --> 00:47:23,114
It is the favor of Allah on you, you shouldn't come and brag about it to Muhammadﷺ

633
00:47:23,138 --> 00:47:25,232
by saying that we have done you a favor by becoming Muslim.

634
00:47:25,845 --> 00:47:29,579
 It is a favor from Allah that He allowed you to become Muslim

635
00:47:29,950 --> 00:47:31,978
 that He guided to the straight path anyway.

636
00:47:32,912 --> 00:47:36,537
Tulaiha Al-Asdi(طليحة ألأسدي), later on changed his mind and he claimed to be a prophet.

637
00:47:37,986 --> 00:47:42,781
Because when they were in the desert, and they had no water

638
00:47:43,550 --> 00:47:48,498
someone riding on the camel of Tulaiha Al-Asdi(طليحة ألأسدي) found water,

639
00:47:48,538 --> 00:47:52,804
 so they considered to be a blessed camel, belonging to a blessed person

640
00:47:53,082 --> 00:47:56,981
he took advantage of that and he claimed that he is a prophet of Allah.

641
00:47:58,157 --> 00:48:02,001
And again he would make this funny, Su'ar(سوئر), just like Musailimah Al-Kazzab(مسيلمة ألكذاب)

642
00:48:02,959 --> 00:48:09,986
Tulaiha Al-Asdi(طليحة ألأسدي) was a very courageous man, strong fighter, very skilled leader.

643
00:48:10,896 --> 00:48:14,184
So, that claim was very dangerous to come from such a man

644
00:48:15,243 --> 00:48:17,617
Tulaiha Al-Asdi(طليحة ألأسدي) convinces his people Asd(أسد)

645
00:48:18,551 --> 00:48:24,189
and then they got into a agreement with Ghatafan(غطفان), so Ghatafan(غطفان) join in

646
00:48:24,583 --> 00:48:28,827
and then they were reinforced by Abs(عبس) and Dhabiyan(ذبيان).

647
00:48:29,057 --> 00:48:33,207
So now I have these four huge tribes, all under the leadership of Tulaiha(طليحة).

648
00:48:34,235 --> 00:48:40,004
Now by the way, with all of these new prophets that are springing up everywhere.

649
00:48:40,774 --> 00:48:46,038
 It's not that the Arabs were religious people, it's not that they had conviction in these prophets

650
00:48:46,894 --> 00:48:51,727
 the nature of the Bedouin people is that they are not religious

651
00:48:52,177 --> 00:48:56,992
and people think I mean, you have this assumption that the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) were very religious

652
00:48:57,273 --> 00:49:01,184
and that's why they were very antagonistic towards Islam, that was the furthest from the truth.

653
00:49:01,789 --> 00:49:04,816
The people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), were not very religious

654
00:49:05,703 --> 00:49:08,613
and they were also very tolerant towards religion.

655
00:49:09,617 --> 00:49:11,676
And this is something that people don't realize.

656
00:49:12,532 --> 00:49:18,476
In general, the Arabs were among the most tolerant people, when it comes to religious practice.

657
00:49:19,598 --> 00:49:24,015
In other parts of the world, it was expected that everybody follow the same religion

658
00:49:24,687 --> 00:49:28,753
Homogeneous societies in Persia, Zoroastrians.

659
00:49:29,601 --> 00:49:32,345
Among the Romans, they would persecute the non Christian

660
00:49:32,631 --> 00:49:34,592
the Jews were persecuted in the Holy Land

661
00:49:34,736 --> 00:49:37,161
 so it was expected that everybody follows the same religion.

662
00:49:37,185 --> 00:49:41,310
while in Arabia, like for example in the Yemen, you had Jews, You had Christians

663
00:49:41,674 --> 00:49:46,044
 with these prostitutes, the most famous among them and the leader of this movement

664
00:49:46,068 --> 00:49:49,051
which was called the movement of prostitutes, was a Jew.

665
00:49:49,556 --> 00:49:51,543
Her name was Hirr Bin Yamin Al-Yahoodia(هربنت يامين اليهودية)

666
00:49:52,086 --> 00:49:55,987
and in fact this prostitute she set a record in prostitution

667
00:49:56,011 --> 00:49:58,522
that she became an example, they would say;

668
00:49:58,562 --> 00:49:59,098
أذنا من هر

669
00:49:59,747 --> 00:50:01,973
Whenever a woman would be accused with this, they would say

670
00:50:01,997 --> 00:50:03,792
that she is more of a prostitute than Hirr(هر).

671
00:50:06,358 --> 00:50:10,684
So you had Jews in Yemen, you had Christians, you had pagan worshippers

672
00:50:10,708 --> 00:50:14,570
and you had Zoroastrians the Persians, and people were very tolerant about it.

673
00:50:14,996 --> 00:50:17,263
In Makkah Waraqah Bin Nofal(ورقه بن نوفل) was a Christian

674
00:50:18,165 --> 00:50:22,204
Zaid(زيد) was a Hanifi(حنيفي) following the religion of Ibrahim عليه السّلام

675
00:50:22,529 --> 00:50:26,411
and then you had people who didn't follow religion at all, Ad-Dahriyoon(ألدهريون).

676
00:50:26,899 --> 00:50:31,749
In fact, Ukaaz(عكاظ), where the speakers would go and talk about everything

677
00:50:32,136 --> 00:50:33,795
was no different than Hyde Park.

678
00:50:36,393 --> 00:50:38,801
It was a very tolerant society when it came to religion.

679
00:50:39,806 --> 00:50:43,467
Zaid Bin Nufail(زيدبن نفيل) when, he would stand next to Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه)

680
00:50:43,830 --> 00:50:47,082
 and tell the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), that your religion is false.

681
00:50:48,234 --> 00:50:49,455
لستم على شئ

682
00:50:49,897 --> 00:50:54,323
And he would tell them, you should not sacrifice to these idols, and nobody would harm him.

683
00:50:55,741 --> 00:51:01,199
It was only when the Da'wah(دعوة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ began that they became intolerant.

684
00:51:01,579 --> 00:51:06,451
So, a very tolerant society can become very intolerant when it comes to Islam.

685
00:51:07,080 --> 00:51:09,758
So don't be fooled by what you see,

686
00:51:10,687 --> 00:51:12,805
the people of Makkah turned upside down

687
00:51:13,369 --> 00:51:18,591
one of the most tolerant societies in the world when it comes to religion became the most intolerant.

688
00:51:19,028 --> 00:51:19,656
Why?

689
00:51:19,774 --> 00:51:24,489
Because now they're not just dealing with a religion, they're dealing with the truth.

690
00:51:25,473 --> 00:51:30,624
And they know that when the truth comes, it's either truth or falsehood.

691
00:51:30,852 --> 00:51:36,502
 The two cannot coexist, evil can get along with evil, it's just a different brand.

692
00:51:37,178 --> 00:51:41,023
But when it's Al-Haqq(ألحق), it's either Al-Haqq(ألحق) or a Batil(باطل).

693
00:51:41,582 --> 00:51:46,086
So, these tribes were joining Tulaiha Al-Asdi(طليحة ألأزدي) out of nationalism, tribalism.

694
00:51:47,028 --> 00:51:49,437
They didn't want to submit to a man from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

695
00:51:50,184 --> 00:51:53,097
I mean, before it was a Prophet but now Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), who is Abu Bakr(ابوبكر)?

696
00:51:53,508 --> 00:51:56,034
We're not gonna give Baiyah(بَيْعة) to Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق).

697
00:51:58,139 --> 00:51:58,902
Who is he?

698
00:51:59,608 --> 00:52:02,656
 So, they came under the banner of Tulaiha Al-Asdi(طليحة ألأسدي).

699
00:52:03,245 --> 00:52:06,978
Now, Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) for this important mission

700
00:52:07,982 --> 00:52:09,721
عقد الراية لِخالد إبن وليد

701
00:52:10,155 --> 00:52:13,164
He gave the Raiyah(راية), the banner to Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد).

702
00:52:14,153 --> 00:52:18,589
The man whom Rasool Allah ﷺ said about, he is a sword of the swords of Allah

703
00:52:18,883 --> 00:52:22,038
which was drawn against Al-Kuffar(ألكفار) and Al-Munafiqeen(مُنافقين).

704
00:52:22,495 --> 00:52:26,828
سيف من سيوف الله سلّه الله على الكفار والمنافقين

705
00:52:28,395 --> 00:52:34,492
He gave the banner to a man, who never ever had one of his banners in war fall down.

706
00:52:35,792 --> 00:52:38,888
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) has never ever in his life

707
00:52:38,912 --> 00:52:42,781
whether in Islam or before Islam lost in the battle, never.

708
00:52:44,543 --> 00:52:47,007
He sent him to fight Tulaiha(طليحة).

709
00:52:48,457 --> 00:52:51,622
 And Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه told Udae Bin Hatim(عدئ بن حاتم)

710
00:52:52,470 --> 00:52:59,491
go and save your people Tae(طيئ), lest Tulaiha(طليحة) should mislead them.

711
00:53:00,487 --> 00:53:05,523
The tribe of Tae(طيئ), which were neighboring the territory of Tulaiha(طليحة)

712
00:53:06,496 --> 00:53:08,631
had not joined in with Tulaiha(طليحة) yet.

713
00:53:09,862 --> 00:53:13,319
So Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) wants Udae(عديئ), who was the chief of his tribe

714
00:53:13,394 --> 00:53:17,679
 to go as soon as possible, and save his people from hellfire.

715
00:53:19,574 --> 00:53:21,142
 Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said;

716
00:53:21,166 --> 00:53:24,158
أدرك قومك لا  يلحقوا بطليحة فيكون دمارهم

717
00:53:24,967 --> 00:53:28,259
Hasten towards your people, and save them from Tulaiha(طليحة)

718
00:53:28,505 --> 00:53:30,461
because that will be their detriment.

719
00:53:31,247 --> 00:53:34,502
For Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) the issue was already done, Tulaiha(طليحة) is going to lose.

720
00:53:35,647 --> 00:53:39,771
So he's telling Udae(عدئ) go and save your people before they perish.

721
00:53:40,368 --> 00:53:44,442
It wasn't a 50, 50 thing for Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) he already knew the results.

722
00:53:44,923 --> 00:53:47,478
 If you join Tulaiha(طليحة), you're on the losing side.

723
00:53:48,115 --> 00:53:50,069
So he told Udae(عدئ), go and save them.

724
00:53:50,132 --> 00:53:53,190
And Udae Bin Hatim(عدئ بن حاتم), was a Muslim

725
00:53:53,631 --> 00:53:56,883
who came and pledged his Islam to Rasool Allah ﷺ, so he's among the Sahabah(صحابه)

726
00:53:57,255 --> 00:54:01,959
he was the man who came in, wearing the cross, Udae(عدئ) was a Christian

727
00:54:02,807 --> 00:54:06,102
he was wearing a cross, when it came to meet Muhammadﷺ.

728
00:54:06,989 --> 00:54:10,968
So when Rasool Allah ﷺ saw the cross hanging on his chest. He said:

729
00:54:10,992 --> 00:54:14,495
اتَّخَذُوا أَحْبَارَهُمْ وَرُهْبَانَهُمْ أَرْبَابًا مِّن دُونِ اللَّهِ

730
00:54:15,046 --> 00:54:19,512
They have taken their rabbis and their priests gods besides Allah.

731
00:54:20,344 --> 00:54:23,748
Udae(عدئ) said: We do not consider our priests to be gods

732
00:54:24,275 --> 00:54:27,585
Udae(عدئ) is trying to correct the information of Rasool Allah ﷺ about Christianity.

733
00:54:28,292 --> 00:54:31,492
He said: We do not consider our priests to be God.

734
00:54:32,684 --> 00:54:33,833
 Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

735
00:54:34,678 --> 00:54:38,619
These priests, didn't they make, what was Halal(حلال), Haram(حرام)

736
00:54:38,795 --> 00:54:39,979
and what was Haram(حرام), Halal(حلال).

737
00:54:41,007 --> 00:54:44,569
What Allah made legal they made illegal, and what Allah made illegal they made legal.

738
00:54:45,049 --> 00:54:48,138
Udae(عدئ) said: Yes! He said that is worshipping them besides Allah.

739
00:54:50,861 --> 00:54:55,246
When St. Paul says that all of the law of the Bible is dissolved now

740
00:54:55,367 --> 00:54:57,666
you don't have to follow the law of the Torah(توراة).

741
00:54:57,967 --> 00:55:00,236
What is that? It's making Haram(حرام), Halal(حلال).

742
00:55:01,893 --> 00:55:04,675
When Eesa Ibn Maryam(عيسى إبن مريم) says that I came to fulfill the law

743
00:55:04,968 --> 00:55:07,525
Jot by Jot, Dot by Dot, Letter by Letter

744
00:55:07,820 --> 00:55:10,449
and then St. Paul comes on over rules that

745
00:55:10,694 --> 00:55:13,488
 and says; No! You don't have to follow the law,

746
00:55:14,758 --> 00:55:17,766
that is worshiping Him, besides Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

747
00:55:19,532 --> 00:55:24,802
Going back to the issue of the religion of the Arabs, the northern tribes were Christian.

748
00:55:25,834 --> 00:55:30,185
So Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) was asked about eating their meat because they're a Christian.

749
00:55:30,453 --> 00:55:31,548
 Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) said;

750
00:55:31,924 --> 00:55:36,649
They know nothing about Christianity but drinking wine, thats all, they know about it.

751
00:55:36,910 --> 00:55:38,797
ليس لهم من النصراني ألأشرب من الخمر

752
00:55:39,495 --> 00:55:41,612
These people are not religious, they're not into religion.

753
00:55:43,336 --> 00:55:46,897
So, Udae Bin Hatim(عدئ بن حاتم) went to plead with his people

754
00:55:49,003 --> 00:55:51,110
and he told Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد): Give me three days

755
00:55:51,396 --> 00:55:53,792
because Khalid(خالد) was ready to attack Tae(طئ)

756
00:55:54,756 --> 00:56:01,130
Udae(عدئ) said: Wait, because Tae(طئ) have already sent some fighters to join with Tulaiha(طليحة),

757
00:56:01,296 --> 00:56:07,921
so they were already stuck not all of them but they have already sent some of their men to fight alongside Tulaiha(طليحة).

758
00:56:08,106 --> 00:56:10,048
So, Khalid(خالد) was ready to attack them. Udae(عدئ) said:

759
00:56:10,178 --> 00:56:12,578
Just give me three days, and then he told Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد)

760
00:56:13,075 --> 00:56:17,208
isn't it better that I saved them from hellfire.?

761
00:56:18,338 --> 00:56:24,124
Would you rather have them go to hell, or be saved from hell, and not fight you.

762
00:56:25,457 --> 00:56:27,476
So Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) said: I will give you three days

763
00:56:27,826 --> 00:56:30,056
so Udae(عدئ) went, his people said:

764
00:56:30,080 --> 00:56:34,835
We are never going to pledge allegiance to the father of the young camel, Abul Faseel(أبوالفصيل).

765
00:56:35,678 --> 00:56:40,871
Because I said, that Bakr(بكر) means young camel that's full of vigor

766
00:56:41,656 --> 00:56:45,791
but they were calling him Abul Faseel(أبوالفصيل), Faseel(فصيل) is a newborn camel, that is weak.

767
00:56:46,743 --> 00:56:50,102
So they were nicknaming Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), the father of the weak camel,

768
00:56:50,266 --> 00:56:52,573
they considered him to be a weak man. They said:

769
00:56:52,787 --> 00:56:58,706
We, the people Tae(طئ), you want us to pledge allegiance to the father of the young camel.

770
00:56:58,730 --> 00:57:05,767
Udae Bin Hatim(عدئ بن حاتم) said: Listen, his armies are gonna start coming to your land one after another,

771
00:57:06,140 --> 00:57:11,065
 and they will teach you a lesson that is the father of the stallion and not the father of the young camel.

772
00:57:12,146 --> 00:57:14,886
 Listen to me, and give your Baiyah(بَيْعة) to him.

773
00:57:15,704 --> 00:57:16,653
They refused.

774
00:57:16,907 --> 00:57:23,344
He stayed there, trying, going back and forth negotiating with them convincing them for three days

775
00:57:23,424 --> 00:57:26,409
until he was able to convince one branch of Tae(طئ).

776
00:57:26,709 --> 00:57:29,805
Tae(طئ) were made of two branches, he convinced one.

777
00:57:30,072 --> 00:57:31,242
He went back to Khalid(خالد) and said:

778
00:57:31,266 --> 00:57:35,050
Give me some time, because I've saved one branch, give me some time to save the other.

779
00:57:35,359 --> 00:57:36,495
Khalid(خالد) said: Go ahead.

780
00:57:36,738 --> 00:57:42,385
He went tried his best with them and he was able to pull them out of the alliance with Tulaiha(طليحة).

781
00:57:43,110 --> 00:57:47,117
Now they said: We have to call our fighters from the army of Tulaiha(طليحة)

782
00:57:47,334 --> 00:57:51,931
because if Tulaiha(طليحة) hears that we are Muslim now, he's gonna kill our men

783
00:57:52,493 --> 00:57:55,198
and they were able to withdraw those also.

784
00:57:55,893 --> 00:57:57,144
So Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر) says that

785
00:57:57,168 --> 00:58:01,097
Udae Bin Hatim(عدئ بن حاتم) was considered to be the most blessed man for his people.

786
00:58:01,719 --> 00:58:03,275
He saved them from hellfire.

787
00:58:04,204 --> 00:58:08,388
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) sent out two of the Sahabah(صحابه)

788
00:58:09,244 --> 00:58:14,777
on a reconnaissance mission to go and gather information about the army of Tulaiha(طليحة).

789
00:58:15,031 --> 00:58:16,878
These two companions were Ukasha Bin Muhsan(عكاشة بن محصن)

790
00:58:17,404 --> 00:58:19,734
and Sabit Bin Qais Bin Shammas(ثابت بن قيس بن شماس)

791
00:58:19,821 --> 00:58:21,263
two among the prominent Sahabah(صحابه).

792
00:58:21,907 --> 00:58:26,491
Tulaiha Al-Asdi(طليحة ألأزدي) and his brother were out, also, spying on the Muslims.

793
00:58:27,041 --> 00:58:32,836
 Tulaiha(طليحة) again, was a very courageous man, he went out by himself, he and his brother alone

794
00:58:34,018 --> 00:58:39,674
and they killed Ukasha(عكاشة) and Sabit Bin Qais(ثابت بن قيس).

795
00:58:40,344 --> 00:58:43,232
So when they didn't come back, Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) and the army went to investigate

796
00:58:43,256 --> 00:58:45,607
and they came and found the two bodies of the Sahabah(صحابه)

797
00:58:45,996 --> 00:58:49,595
it says in the book of history that that was a very great setback for the Muslims.

798
00:58:50,193 --> 00:58:54,460
It hurt them a lot, to lose two of the great companions of Rasool Allah ﷺ

799
00:58:54,498 --> 00:58:56,053
in a moment, just like that.

800
00:58:57,383 --> 00:58:59,481
So it was very difficult moment for the Muslims.

801
00:59:01,372 --> 00:59:08,055
But Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) made his move, and they attacked, and they succeeded in defeating Tulaiha Al-Asdi(طليحة ألسدي).

802
00:59:08,248 --> 00:59:11,550
Now Tulaiha(طليحة) among his alliance was Oyeyna Bin Hasan(عيينة بن حصن)

803
00:59:11,571 --> 00:59:16,263
Oyeyna Bin Hasan(عيينة بن حصن) was among the men, who came and gave pledge of allegiance to Rasool Ullah

804
00:59:16,284 --> 00:59:19,731
and then they broke it and came again, these men would go back and forth

805
00:59:20,240 --> 00:59:22,230
the Bedouins in and out.

806
00:59:22,674 --> 00:59:25,843
So Oyeyna Bin Hasan(عيينة بن حصن) he made an alliance with Tulaiha(طليحة).

807
00:59:26,333 --> 00:59:31,038
So, while the fighting was going on, Tulaiha Al-Asdi(طليحة ألأزدي) was sitting in his tent,

808
00:59:31,405 --> 00:59:32,993
waiting for revelation to come to him.

809
00:59:33,458 --> 00:59:36,681
So Oyeyna(عيينة) come to him and said: Did you receive Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) yet, he said: No!

810
00:59:37,100 --> 00:59:39,976
Went and fought, he came back, did Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) come yet, No!

811
00:59:40,781 --> 00:59:43,690
He came third time. Did Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) come, he said: Yes!

812
00:59:43,930 --> 00:59:48,098
What did he tell you? He said: I'm giving you a millstone and some great news

813
00:59:48,455 --> 00:59:53,638
Oyeyna(عيينة) was not waiting for such a revelation he was waiting for something else, tell us what to do.?

814
00:59:54,212 --> 00:59:57,504
He said: Well, you're going to get some great news. Oyeyna(عيينة) left

815
00:59:57,528 --> 00:59:59,717
and he told all of his fighters, to just leave.

816
01:00:00,570 --> 01:00:03,221
And that was the beginning of the end for Tulaiha(طليحة)

817
01:00:03,519 --> 01:00:05,353
When Tulaiha(طليحة) realized that he's losing.

818
01:00:05,652 --> 01:00:13,570
He and his brother and his wife and some of his close friends, mounted their camels and horses and ran away to Iraq and Ash-Sham(ألشام).

819
01:00:14,698 --> 01:00:17,864
And that was the end of Tulaiha Al-Asdi(طليحة ألأسدي).

820
01:00:18,825 --> 01:00:23,641
Now, the news reached Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), this was a great victory.

821
01:00:24,107 --> 01:00:25,773
 He sent a letter to Khalid(خالد) telling him.

822
01:00:26,402 --> 01:00:30,361
May that which Allah has granted you by way of blessings, increase for you.

823
01:00:31,295 --> 01:00:37,778
Fear Allah in your affairs for verily, Allah is with those, who are pious and who do good works

824
01:00:38,196 --> 01:00:41,635
take seriously the Command of Allah and be not lenient.

825
01:00:42,232 --> 01:00:46,583
And whoever you lay your hands over from the disbelievers, who fought the Muslims

826
01:00:47,041 --> 01:00:50,766
then severely punished them and make them as an example to warn another.

827
01:00:51,403 --> 01:00:56,403
So kill whomever you like of those, who showed enmity to Allah, or who opposed Him.

828
01:00:56,759 --> 01:00:59,187
If you think there will be some benefit in doing so.

829
01:00:59,923 --> 01:01:05,906
So, due to these orders from Al-Khalifah(ألخليفه) to severely punish the Murtaddeen(مرتدين)

830
01:01:05,930 --> 01:01:07,555
and to make an example out of them.

831
01:01:08,015 --> 01:01:11,402
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) remained in the territory for entire month

832
01:01:11,626 --> 01:01:15,749
going up and down, right and left, capturing the Murtaddeen(مرتدين)

833
01:01:16,292 --> 01:01:20,559
 and killing them by burning them in the fire, stoning them to death

834
01:01:21,017 --> 01:01:24,513
throwing them from mountaintops, throwing them into wells

835
01:01:24,814 --> 01:01:28,328
and piercing them with arrows, very harsh punishment

836
01:01:28,668 --> 01:01:31,734
but he was doing it to set an example to the rest of the Murtaddeen(مرتدين)

837
01:01:32,215 --> 01:01:34,247
that Riddah(ردَّة) will not be tolerated.

838
01:01:35,482 --> 01:01:41,206
Al-Fujja'a(ألفجاء) was one of these man who came to Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

839
01:01:42,546 --> 01:01:47,406
And he said: I'm going to fight the Murtaddeen(مرتدين), Give me an army

840
01:01:48,123 --> 01:01:51,568
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) provided him with camels and weapons

841
01:01:52,116 --> 01:01:58,583
Al-Fujja'a(ألفجاء), left, and he used the arms and camels that were given to him by the Khalifah(خليفه)

842
01:01:58,894 --> 01:02:06,933
 to fight everyone whom he meets Muslim or non Muslim to raid their belongings, a bandit in the desert.

843
01:02:07,790 --> 01:02:12,417
When Al-Khalifah(خليفه) heard of that he sent an army to follow him; in pursue.

844
01:02:13,017 --> 01:02:17,740
They did capture Al-Fujja'a(ألفجاء), and they brought him back to Madina tied up,

845
01:02:17,970 --> 01:02:25,644
so Al-Khalifah(خليفه) ordered that he be burnt to death, in Al-Baqiyyah(ألبقية) in front of everyone

846
01:02:26,054 --> 01:02:27,919
as a punishment for his action.

847
01:02:30,509 --> 01:02:34,348
Tulaiha(طليحة) later became Muslim, he regretted what he did.

848
01:02:35,517 --> 01:02:38,311
 And he made Umra(عمرة) during the time of Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق).

849
01:02:38,343 --> 01:02:41,192
So, they told Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), Tulaiha(طليحة) is here.

850
01:02:42,404 --> 01:02:45,709
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) said: What should I do with him, he already became Muslim

851
01:02:47,291 --> 01:02:51,202
but again he was banned from participating in any of the Muslim armies.

852
01:02:51,992 --> 01:02:54,846
Later on, after that he did join in the Fatoohaat(فتوحات)

853
01:02:55,611 --> 01:02:59,798
and he set some amazing examples of courage and bravery Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

854
01:03:01,669 --> 01:03:05,419
So Allah could guide whomever He wishes. This is a man, who claimed prophethood

855
01:03:05,884 --> 01:03:11,629
because of him, hundreds of people went to hellfire and then eventually, he became Muslim.

856
01:03:12,672 --> 01:03:14,662
See with Hidaya(هداية), it's Qadar(قَدَر) of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

857
01:03:16,010 --> 01:03:21,327
Abu Talib(ابوطالب), who assisted Rasool Allah ﷺ for all of his life goes to hellfire

858
01:03:22,042 --> 01:03:25,888
and Abu Sufiyan(أبوسُفيان), who fights Rasool Allah ﷺ for all of his life becomes a Mo'min(مؤمن).

859
01:03:27,098 --> 01:03:29,161
The Hidaya(هداية) is something in hands on Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

860
01:03:30,905 --> 01:03:33,735
Asd(أسد) and Ghatafan(غطفان) regretted what they have done

861
01:03:34,250 --> 01:03:35,752
when Tulaiha(طليحة) has deserted them,

862
01:03:36,105 --> 01:03:41,336
and they came to the Khalifah(خليفه) Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

863
01:03:42,074 --> 01:03:47,236
And they wanted to make Toba(توبة), they came to the Khalifah(خليفه) and said:

864
01:03:47,784 --> 01:03:51,289
We want to make a truce between you and us.

865
01:03:52,030 --> 01:03:53,240
What did the Khalifah(خليفه) say.?

866
01:03:53,815 --> 01:03:57,741
He said: I give you one of two options, that's all what I have for you.

867
01:03:58,354 --> 01:04:01,707
فأما الحرب المجلية أو الخطة المخزية

868
01:04:02,674 --> 01:04:08,425
Either a war of extermination, or a humiliating plan.

869
01:04:09,150 --> 01:04:13,291
They said: We know what the war of extermination means, it means that you get rid of all of us

870
01:04:13,420 --> 01:04:16,828
but what does the humiliating deal mean?

871
01:04:17,207 --> 01:04:23,883
He said: Number one, you give up all of your weapons and you follow the tails of your camels.

872
01:04:25,676 --> 01:04:30,611
You know, to them, stripping them of their weapons is dishonoring them.

873
01:04:31,076 --> 01:04:34,426
Now, with Muslims, it's not an issue people are living like that

874
01:04:34,450 --> 01:04:38,324
they don't see it the problem, but with them even though in the time of Jahiliyyah(جَاهلِيَّة)

875
01:04:38,953 --> 01:04:41,099
living without your weapons is dishonor.

876
01:04:41,123 --> 01:04:43,796
So he says it's like you and your camel are one of the same

877
01:04:44,879 --> 01:04:47,105
without your arms, you are no different than the camel.

878
01:04:47,390 --> 01:04:50,875
He said: You give up your arms and you follow the tails of your camels.

879
01:04:51,691 --> 01:04:57,574
Until Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ puts in the heart of the Khalifah(خليفه) of Rasool Allah ﷺ and the Mo'mineen(مؤمنين)

880
01:04:58,153 --> 01:04:59,424
to accept your apology.

881
01:05:00,376 --> 01:05:02,067
So your hand down all every weapons

882
01:05:02,408 --> 01:05:08,383
and then whenever Allah makes the Khalifah(خليفه) and the Mo'mineen(مؤمنين) accept your apology.

883
01:05:08,407 --> 01:05:10,317
 We'll go ahead with it, but I cannot promise you, when.!

884
01:05:11,813 --> 01:05:19,188
Number two, you declare publicly that the ones, who are killed among you are going to hell fire.

885
01:05:19,926 --> 01:05:22,376
 And the ones, who are killed among us are going to Jannah(جنة).

886
01:05:23,278 --> 01:05:26,381
I want to hear that from you publicly in front of everyone, in front of your people.

887
01:05:28,088 --> 01:05:33,389
Number three, you pay blood money for the ones, who killed among us

888
01:05:33,413 --> 01:05:36,103
and we pay you nothing for the ones we killed among you.

889
01:05:36,787 --> 01:05:40,611
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: I disagree with this last point.

890
01:05:41,194 --> 01:05:43,643
He said: They should not pay us blood money

891
01:05:44,022 --> 01:05:46,760
because the ones, who are killed among us are Shuhadaa(شهداء)

892
01:05:46,968 --> 01:05:48,311
and they died in the path of Allah.

893
01:05:49,690 --> 01:05:52,379
So there is no loss on our behalf - it's an honor for them

894
01:05:53,133 --> 01:05:54,678
but then he said: I like all the rest.

895
01:05:55,151 --> 01:05:57,085
 I mean, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), this is what he wants.

896
01:05:57,109 --> 01:05:59,009
 I mean this. Yeah, fine! Great!

897
01:05:59,604 --> 01:06:04,898
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه gave them a lesson that he is the father of the stallion and not the father of the young camel.

898
01:06:06,818 --> 01:06:11,294
And they had to agree, give up their weapons, following the tails of their camels

899
01:06:12,306 --> 01:06:17,513
until later on your Khalifah(خليفه) will decide when to accept your apology, what you have done.

900
01:06:19,641 --> 01:06:22,615
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

